      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-10T00:16:26Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): a probe-only program's stock sim judges the uncut stock\n\nA touch probe stays out of the program sim's plan (it removes nothing),\nso a probe-only program sized the stock lattice by min(radius) over no\ntools = +inf, and the grid refused the infinite cell as \"invalid stock\nsimulation setup: ... box non-empty ...\" - the wrong cause, shown on\nevery probe-only post. stock_grid now sizes the lattice by the stock's\nspan when no tool radius is finite; the sim judges the uncut stock\n(clean when it is the part). A missing or invalid stock still refuses\nby its own name.\n\nPinned by probe_only_sim::a_probe_only_program_is_judged_not_refused_as_an_invalid_setup\n(fails without the fix) and ::a_probe_only_program_without_a_stock_still_says_why.\n\nFixes #592\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
